  "user_id": 18762,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "Try to complete as many AI Design Challenges as you can! Expand each challenge for more information and tips for each challenge. \r\n\r\n:::details [**Challenge 1: Revise the page content**]\r\n\r\nCan you figure out how to change your webpage to a different topic of your choice?\r\n- What is your page about?\r\n- What sections or components should it include?\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**Challenge 2: Style it**]\r\n\r\nCan you figure out how to change the CSS to give your page a different color scheme or visual style?\r\n- A new color theme\r\n- A different visual style (modern, bold, simple, etc)\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**Challenge 3: Add images**]\r\n\r\nCan you figure out how to add images from the `images` folder in the file panel?\r\n- Use image file names\r\n- Tell AI where to place them\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**Challenge 4: Design for the user**]\r\n\r\nSam uses your app outside in bright sunlight. \r\n\r\nCan you figure out how to improve the page so it works better for Sam?\r\n- Think about readability and contrast\r\n- Make buttons and text easy to see\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**Challenge 5: Experiment like a Designer**]\r\n\r\nCan you ask the AI to make a major design change to your page?\r\n\r\nTry:\r\n- Changing the layout\r\n- Turning your images into gallery cards\r\n- Adding a new section\r\n- Redesigning the page style\r\n\r\n:::\r\n",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Students may try to edit the code directly**  \r\n- Some students may click into the HTML or CSS and try to make changes themselves. Gently redirect them to use AI by asking: *“Can you ask the AI to make that change instead?”* The goal is to guide AI, not write code.\r\n\r\n**Students may use vague prompts and get poor results**  \r\n- Students may type short prompts like “change it” or “make it better.” Encourage them to be more specific by asking: *“What exactly do you want the page to look like?”* Remind them that clearer prompts lead to better results.\r\n\r\n**Students may accept AI output without reviewing it**  \r\n- Students may quickly accept changes without checking the result. Prompt them to preview and reflect first: *“Does this match what you expected?”* Reinforce that they are responsible for deciding whether the AI’s output is good enough.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
